title ALES111 — Lotus's crop, the exact complement of cut (trim to selection)
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES110 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think ALES2's cut removes the named span and keeps everything around it — the clip SHRINKS by exactly the span. Its exact complement is crop: keep the named span and remove everything else — the clip BECOMES the span. Trim to Selection / Crop is the button every editor ships (circle the one phrase worth keeping, drop the rest). Where cut answers remove this, crop answers keep only this; the two partition every edit of a span into its two honest readings. Naming crop beside cut completes that pair — a clean, Lindy-durable primitive absent from the suite (checked: no crop/keep-only exists; center_clip's "crop" is amplitude clipping, a different sense).
think Shape: crop(clip, start, count) slides the kept span [start, start+count) to the front in one bounded FORWARD pass (dest index i is always <= src index start+i since start >= 0, so no live sample is overwritten before it is read), then sets the length to count. Reuses timeline.EditError whole — BadRange when start > len or count > len - start, checked without underflow (count against the remainder), refused before any write. No allocation, no second buffer.
think Four laws: the CROP law (the clip becomes original[start .. start+count) byte for byte, the length exactly count, proven at mid/head/tail); the COMPLEMENT law — the crux tying it to ALES2: crop yields the middle span, cut yields the head-plus-tail around it, and splicing the crop back at start into the cut reconstructs the source byte for byte (proven side by side over ALES2's own cut and splice); the SUBSET / PEAK law (crop only drops, so the peak re-measured through ALES13 is non-increasing — cropping away the loudest sample strictly lowers it, cropping a span that still holds it holds it); the DEGENERATE / REFUSAL law (crop(0, len) the identity, crop(start, 0) the empty clip, the empty clip its own crop, a start past the samples or a count past the remainder BadRange, the clip verified untouched after each refused call).
obs Witness GREEN on the first pass — all four laws and both refusal branches, the clip verified untouched after each refused call. The complement law is the crux of the teaching: proving crop and cut PARTITION the span (splice the crop back into the cut, recover the source) makes the remove/keep-only pair read as one closed idea rather than two unrelated edits. Forward copy is safe by construction (start >= 0 keeps dest at or behind src) — asserted in the invariant note, no reverse-direction guard needed as cut required for its tail shift. TAME style bans clean (ratchet zero-assert count unchanged); >=2 positive-invariant asserts per fn; width-check clean; no new arithmetic invented; timeline.EditError reused whole. No custody gate touched — pure-Rye local i16 buffer, siloed to lotus/.
loom witness=ales_crop_witness green=1 laws=4 rung=ALES111
